questions.prompt:
This Node handler adds a like. Under load, the count ends up much lower than the number of clicks. Explain why and give **two** different fixes.

```js
app.post('/posts/:id/like', async (req, res) => {
  const { rows } = await db.query('SELECT likes FROM posts WHERE id = $1', [req.params.id]);
  const likes = rows[0].likes + 1;
  await db.query('UPDATE posts SET likes = $1 WHERE id = $2', [likes, req.params.id]);
  res.json({ likes });
});
```

questions.answer:
```js
app.post('/posts/:id/like', async (req, res) => {
  const { rows } = await db.query(
    'UPDATE posts SET likes = likes + 1 WHERE id = $1 RETURNING likes',
    [req.params.id]
  );
  res.json({ likes: rows[0].likes });
});
```
The read and write now happen in one atomic statement, so concurrent likes cannot overwrite each other.
